Inheritance - IS - A - Relationship

A pillar of Object oriented programming as it allows the creation of 
hierarchical classifications.

How and when to achieve Inheritance:-
You can create a general class that defines the traits commom to a set of related items. - Parent class/ super class

This class will then be inherited by other, more specific classes. these 
specific classes add those things that are unique to it. - child class / 
sub class

Note - In java terminology, a class that is inherited is called super class.
The class that does the inheriting is called a sub class.
Hence, a sub-class is a specialized version of a super class.
A sub-class inherits all of the members defined by the super-class and add its own unique elements.

To inherit a class, you simply incorporate the definition of one class
into another by using the "extends" keyword.

